@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il04-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il34-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-s341-order-5759-1999`

-- TESTS for s 341 and the Order of 5759-1999 (row IL-34, priority 2). Expected values worked by hand from the
-- Hebrew text before the run.
--   s 341: an order is validly made if the Minister made it and the Finance Committee approved it (both).
--   Order s 3: began 1.1.1999, applies to contributions payable for that day and after.
--   Order s 4: from the commencement day to 31.3.2000, s 1 reaches an employee as well.
--   Order s 1: the amount is the year's reduced collection threshold (7,703 in 2026, the Institute's published
--     figure carried by row IL-04); a quarter's amount is declined by default and 3 x 7,703 = 23,109 at the
--     named reading.

§ `Tests: section 341 and the Order of 5759-1999`

§§ `Section 341: what makes an order valid`

#ASSERT     `s 341 — the order is validly made` (`An order under section 341` WITH `made by the Minister` IS TRUE,  `approved by the Finance Committee of the Knesset` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 341 — the order is validly made` (`An order under section 341` WITH `made by the Minister` IS TRUE,  `approved by the Finance Committee of the Knesset` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 341 — the order is validly made` (`An order under section 341` WITH `made by the Minister` IS FALSE, `approved by the Finance Committee of the Knesset` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 341 — the order is validly made` (`An order under section 341` WITH `made by the Minister` IS FALSE, `approved by the Finance Committee of the Knesset` IS FALSE)

§§ `Order s 3: when it began`

#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 3 — the day it began` EQUALS YMD 1999 1 1
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 3 — the Order applies to contributions payable for the day` (YMD 1999 1 1)
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 3 — the Order applies to contributions payable for the day` (YMD 2026 10 9)
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 3 — the Order applies to contributions payable for the day` (YMD 1998 12 31) BECAUSE "contributions payable for a day before 1 January 1999 are governed by the Order No. 2 of 5747-1987, which is not deposited"

§§ `Order s 4: the temporary reach to an employee`

#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 4 — the last day of the temporary provision` EQUALS YMD 2000 3 31
#ASSERT     `Order of 5759-1999 s 4 — s 1 reaches an employee, by this section alone, on the day` (YMD 1999 1 1)
#ASSERT     `Order of 5759-1999 s 4 — s 1 reaches an employee, by this section alone, on the day` (YMD 2000 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT `Order of 5759-1999 s 4 — s 1 reaches an employee, by this section alone, on the day` (YMD 2000 4 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Order of 5759-1999 s 4 — s 1 reaches an employee, by this section alone, on the day` (YMD 1998 12 31)

-- All three classes from 1.1.1999; none before it (the Order No. 2 of 5747-1987 governed, not deposited).
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 — the Order's amount applies to` `an employee` `on the day` (YMD 1999 6 1)
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 — the Order's amount applies to` `a self-employed person` `on the day` (YMD 1999 6 1)
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 — the Order's amount applies to` `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed` `on the day` (YMD 2026 10 9)
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 — the Order's amount applies to` `an employee` `on the day` (YMD 2000 4 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 — the Order's amount applies to` `an employee` `on the day` (YMD 1998 12 31) BECAUSE "contributions payable for a day before 1 January 1999 are governed by the Order No. 2 of 5747-1987, which is not deposited"

§§ `Order s 1: the amount for a month`

-- Every month of 2026 is 7,703: the threshold moves only on 1 January, so the first month of the quarter gives the year's figure.
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 1 `of` 2026 EQUALS 7_703
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 2 `of` 2026 EQUALS 7_703
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 3 `of` 2026 EQUALS 7_703
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 4 `of` 2026 EQUALS 7_703
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 6 `of` 2026 EQUALS 7_703
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 7 `of` 2026 EQUALS 7_703
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 9 `of` 2026 EQUALS 7_703
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 10 `of` 2026 EQUALS 7_703
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 12 `of` 2026 EQUALS 7_703

-- Both ends of the month number, and the years the sources do not give.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 0 `of` 2026 BECAUSE "a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 13 `of` 2026 BECAUSE "a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 1 `of` 2027 BECAUSE "the reduced collection threshold for 2027 or 2028 had not been published when this encoding was made"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 1 `of` 2029 BECAUSE "the reduced collection threshold from 2029 depends on average wages not known when this encoding was made"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 12 `of` 2025 BECAUSE "the Order's amount from 2006 to 2025 is 60% of the average wage of the quarter's first month, and the monthly series of the average wage for those years is not deposited"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 1 `of` 2006 BECAUSE "the Order's amount from 2006 to 2025 is 60% of the average wage of the quarter's first month, and the monthly series of the average wage for those years is not deposited"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 12 `of` 2005 BECAUSE "the Order's amount from 1999 to 2005 is half the average wage of the quarter's first month, and the monthly series of the average wage for those years is not deposited"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 1 `of` 1999 BECAUSE "the Order's amount from 1999 to 2005 is half the average wage of the quarter's first month, and the monthly series of the average wage for those years is not deposited"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 12 `of` 1998 BECAUSE "contributions payable for a day before 1 January 1999 are governed by the Order No. 2 of 5747-1987, which is not deposited"

§§ `Order s 1: the amount for a quarter (fork O1)`

-- The switch declines: the text does not say how a quarter's amount relates to a month's.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the quarter beginning in month` 1 `of` 2026 BECAUSE "the Order's s 1 does not say how a quarter's amount relates to a month's"
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the reading this row takes of a quarter's amount` EQUALS `a quarter's amount is declined`
-- At the named reading: 3 x 7,703 = 23,109, for each of the four quarters.
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the quarter beginning in month` 1  `of` 2026 `, reading a quarter's amount as` `a quarter's amount is three times a month's` EQUALS 23_109
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the quarter beginning in month` 4  `of` 2026 `, reading a quarter's amount as` `a quarter's amount is three times a month's` EQUALS 23_109
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the quarter beginning in month` 7  `of` 2026 `, reading a quarter's amount as` `a quarter's amount is three times a month's` EQUALS 23_109
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the quarter beginning in month` 10 `of` 2026 `, reading a quarter's amount as` `a quarter's amount is three times a month's` EQUALS 23_109
-- A quarter does not begin in month 2; the year's figure still has to exist.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the quarter beginning in month` 2 `of` 2026 `, reading a quarter's amount as` `a quarter's amount is three times a month's` BECAUSE "a quarter begins in month 1, 4, 7 or 10"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the quarter beginning in month` 1 `of` 2027 `, reading a quarter's amount as` `a quarter's amount is three times a month's` BECAUSE "the reduced collection threshold for 2027 or 2028 had not been published when this encoding was made"

§§ `Order s 1 with the average wage of the quarter's first month given`

-- 2006 to 2025: 60% of the average wage (s 341's last limb before the 2025 Budget-year Law s 19(3)); 60% x 12,536 = 7,521.6, the
-- Institute's 2025 average wage for contributions (7,522 as published, rounded). 1999 to 2005: half. 2026 on: s 334(a), the average wage ignored.
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 12 `of` 2025 `, the average wage of the quarter's first month being` 12_536 EQUALS 7_521.6
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 1 `of` 2006 `, the average wage of the quarter's first month being` 10_000 EQUALS 6_000
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 12 `of` 2005 `, the average wage of the quarter's first month being` 10_000 EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 1 `of` 1999 `, the average wage of the quarter's first month being` 10_000 EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 5 `of` 2026 `, the average wage of the quarter's first month being` 99_999 EQUALS 7_703
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 12 `of` 1998 `, the average wage of the quarter's first month being` 10_000 BECAUSE "contributions payable for a day before 1 January 1999 are governed by the Order No. 2 of 5747-1987, which is not deposited"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 13 `of` 2025 `, the average wage of the quarter's first month being` 12_536 BECAUSE "a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 1 `of` 2027 `, the average wage of the quarter's first month being` 12_536 BECAUSE "the reduced collection threshold for 2027 or 2028 had not been published when this encoding was made"
